<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sushila Karki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1952–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sushila Karki is a Nepalese jurist who became the first woman to serve as chief justice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, in 2016–2017, known for rulings against corruption. In September 2025, after youth-led protests forced the resignation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/k-p-sharma-oli">K. P. Sharma Oli</a>, she was appointed interim prime minister, the first woman to hold the office, with a mandate to hold new elections in March 2026.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sushila-karki.jpg" alt="Sushila Karki" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: US Embassy Kathmandu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sushila_Karki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
